# OTA firmware verification public key — EXAMPLE.
#
# This is a throwaway Ed25519 public key showing the expected format. It does
# NOT match any real signing key; devices provisioned with it will refuse
# every real release.
#
# To provision for real:
#   1. python3 scripts/ota-generate-keys.py
#   2. Set the printed PRIVATE key as the GitHub Actions secret OTA_SIGNING_KEY.
#   3. Commit the printed PUBLIC key as config/ota_public_key.pem (this file's
#      name without ".example").
#
# The OTA agent reads /opt/bluesignal/current/config/ota_public_key.pem
# (falling back to the repo checkout's config/ota_public_key.pem) and ignores
# comment lines above the PEM block. See docs/ota-runbook.md.
-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----
MCowBQYDK2VwAyEAbawF7yX9gY5g8cn2H2f7PXHrzElCDl904ChAmLtaAag=
-----END PUBLIC KEY-----
